  "generated_text": "1. Calculate \\(\\rho\\):\n\\[\n\\rho = \\sqrt{x^2 + y^2 + z^2} = \\sqrt{(2 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 6^2 + (-4)^2} = \\sqrt{12 + 36 + 16} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\n\\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(\\theta\\):\n\\[\n\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{6}{2 \\sqrt{3}}\\right) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right) = \\frac{\\pi}{3}\n\\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(\\phi\\):\n\\[\n\\phi = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{z}{\\rho}\\right) = \\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-4}{8}\\right) = \\cos^{-1}(-0.5)\n\\]\n\nThus, the spherical coordinates are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(8, \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{2\\pi}{3})}",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[(8, pi/3, (2*pi)/3), '(8, \\\\frac{\\\\pi}{3}, \\\\frac{2\\\\pi}{3})']",
    "gold_answer": "We have that $\\rho = \\sqrt{(2 \\sqrt{3})^2 + 6^2 + (-4)^2} = 8.$  We want $\\phi$ to satisfy\n\\[-4 = 8 \\cos \\phi,\\]so $\\phi = \\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.$\n\nWe want $\\theta$ to satisfy\n\\begin{align*}\n2 \\sqrt{3} &= 8 \\sin \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\cos \\theta, \\\\\n6 &= 8 \\sin \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\sin \\theta.\n\\end{align*}Thus, $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3},$ so the spherical coordinates are $\\boxed{\\left( 8, \\frac{\\pi}{3}, \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} \\right)}.$",
    "is_correct": true
  },
